<title>USA: Anicom sets two-for-one stock split.</title>
<headline>Anicom sets two-for-one stock split.</headline>
<dateline>ROSEMONT, Ill. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anicom Inc said on Wednesday that it declared a two-for-one stock split to be effected in the form of a 100 percent stock dividend.</p>
<p>Anicom said in a statement that the company's authorized common stock was increased to 30 million shares from 10 million at a special stockholders meeting.  </p>
<p>The company had said it planned to split its stock, subject to shareholder approval of an increase in the number of authorized shares.</p>
<p>The stock dividend would be payable on October 7 to holders of record as of October 1.</p>
<p>Anicom sells and distributes multimedia technology products.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
